  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 2–5 at.% Zr to MnNiSi-based magnetic-refrigerant alloys will improve mechanical performance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 2–5 at.% Zr will retain a large magnetocaloric effect in MnNiSi-based alloys.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Zr-free MnNiSi-based baseline has good magnetocaloric performance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Zr-free MnNiSi-based baseline has limited mechanical strength and ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention consists of adding approximately 2–5 at.% Zr during synthesis.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A subsequent heat treatment should promote homogeneous Zr distribution and grain refinement.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled solidification and annealing conditions analogous to those used for refractory or medium-entropy alloys can be optimized for MnNiSi-based compositions.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr has a larger atomic radius than Mn, Ni, and Si.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr addition will induce local lattice distortions in MnNiSi-based alloys.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr addition will refine grains or grain boundaries in MnNiSi-based alloys.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr-induced lattice strain will impede dislocation motion through solid-solution strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr will stabilize a refined microstructure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solid-solution strengthening and microstructural refinement will increase yield strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solid-solution strengthening and microstructural refinement will increase ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9506522::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnetocaloric effect is largely governed by the magnetic transition of the MnNiSi phase.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A low Zr addition will not significantly change magnetic entropy change or magnetic transition temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
